---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import ProductCard from '../../../components/ProductCard.astro';
import RegisterForm from '../../../components/RegisterForm.astro';
import Schema from '../../../components/Schema.astro';
import SectionLabel from '../../../components/SectionLabel.astro';
import MegaHeading from '../../../components/MegaHeading.astro';
import ImageSlot from '../../../components/ImageSlot.astro';
import { site } from '../../../lib/site';
import { getProductsByCategory } from '../../../lib/products';
import { itemListSchema } from '../../../lib/schema';

const productsInCategory = getProductsByCategory('rear-wheel-bags');
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Rear Wheel Bags & Spare Tyre Dirty Gear Bags | Hard Routine"
  description="Spare wheel bags for wet, muddy and filthy gear. Welded liner, real drainage, webbing that holds on corrugations. 60L and 90L. Australian designed. Launching early 2027."
  path="/gear/rear-wheel-bags/"
>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', item: `${site.url}/` },
    { name: 'Gear', item: `${site.url}/gear/` },
    { name: 'Rear Wheel Bags' },
  ]} />
  <Schema schema={itemListSchema(productsInCategory.map((p) => ({
    name: p.name,
    url: `${site.url}${p.categoryPath}${p.slug}/`,
  })))} />

  <ImageSlot
    slotName="LIFESTYLE-DUMP-TRACK"
    basePath="/img/dump-feature-spare"
    width={1376}
    height={768}
    alt=""
    minHeight="70svh"
    fullBleed
    class="category-hero"
  >
    <div class="wrap">
      <SectionLabel label="SYSTEM" index="03" light />
      <MegaHeading as="h1" size="lg" class="category-heading" lines={['Dump']} />
      <p class="mono-label category-descriptor">DUMP 60 · DUMP 90 — LAUNCHING {site.launchWindow.toUpperCase()}</p>
    </div>
  </ImageSlot>

  <section class="section-black">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="prose lede">
        A spare wheel bag mounts on your rear-mounted spare and holds the
        gear you don't want in the cabin — wet towels, muddy recovery gear,
        firewood, rubbish.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap section-block">
      <h2>What goes in a rear wheel bag?</h2>
      <p class="prose">Anything wet, dirty, sharp or smelly. In practice that's:</p>
      <ul class="prose">
        <li>Wet towels, swimmers and washing</li>
        <li>Muddy recovery tracks, snatch straps and shackles after a recovery</li>
        <li>Firewood, which drops bark and scratches interior trim</li>
        <li>Rubbish, on tracks where you have to pack it out</li>
        <li>Boots, thongs and anything else covered in sand</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="prose">
        The point is separation. Keeping filth out of the same space as
        bedding, food and clothing is the whole job.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap problem-statement">
      <h2 class="problem-heading">Why do rear wheel bags fail?</h2>
      <div class="problem-copy">
        <p>
          We read every Australian review and forum thread we could find. The
          complaints cluster on three things, and none of them is the fabric.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>The straps.</strong> Attachment is the number one failure.
          Owners report bags detaching at the top, inverting, and dragging
          down the Birdsville Track. Others describe straps as "piddley" and
          difficult to secure. We use 50 mm webbing with steel cam buckles and
          four anchor points, not two.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>The zip fills with dust.</strong> A fine-gauge zip on the
          back of a vehicle on a dirt road will stop working. We use YKK #10
          VISLON — a coarse moulded chain that sheds grit, under a full-length
          storm flap.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>It doesn't drain, or it drains flies in.</strong> Drainage
          holes let water out and blowflies in. One owner described covering
          his own drain holes with fly mesh after a maggot problem. Ours drain
          through mesh-backed eyelets.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap section-block">
      <SectionLabel label="FIELD" index="02" />
      <h2>What size do I need?</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Wheel bag sizing table">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Capacity</th><th scope="col">Suits</th><th scope="col">Typical load</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>DUMP 60</td><td>Most wagons and dual cabs</td><td>Rubbish and wet gear for a weekend</td></tr>
            <tr><td>DUMP 90</td><td>Extended touring, families</td><td>Recovery tracks, firewood, a week's rubbish</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="prose">
        Both fit spare wheels from 16 to 18 inch with tyres up to 285 section
        width. Measure your tyre's overall diameter if you're unsure — it's
        printed on the sidewall.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap section-block">
      <SectionLabel label="MATERIAL" index="03" />
      <h2>Specification</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Specification table">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col"><span class="visually-hidden">Spec</span></th><th scope="col">DUMP 60</th><th scope="col">DUMP 90</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Capacity</th><td>60 L</td><td>90 L</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Dimensions</th><td>550 × 600 × 180 mm</td><td>620 × 700 × 210 mm</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Empty weight</th><td>1.3 kg</td><td>1.6 kg</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Fabric</th><td colspan="2">500D PU-coated nylon oxford</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Liner</th><td colspan="2">Welded TPU, removable, hoses out</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Drainage</th><td>4 mesh-backed eyelets</td><td>6 mesh-backed eyelets</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Zip</th><td colspan="2">YKK #10 VISLON, storm-flapped</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Mounting</th><td colspan="2">50 mm webbing, 4 points, steel cam buckles</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Fits</th><td colspan="2">16–18″ wheels, tyres to 285 section</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap section-block">
      <SectionLabel label="SYSTEM" index="04" />
      <h2>The range</h2>
      <div class="product-grid">
        {productsInCategory.map((p) => <ProductCard product={p} />)}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap section-block">
      <RegisterForm />
    </div>

    <div class="wrap section-block related">
      <h2>Related reading</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/field-notes/dirty-recovery-gear/">How to store recovery gear after you've actually used it</a></li>
        <li><a href="/field-notes/dust-and-zips/">Why dust kills zips, and what to specify instead</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .category-heading { margin-top: var(--space-2); }
  .category-descriptor { margin-top: var(--space-2); color: var(--bone); }

  .lede {
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
    font-size: 19px;
    color: var(--bone-muted);
  }

  .problem-statement { margin-top: var(--space-5); }
  .problem-heading {
    font-size: clamp(30px, 4.2vw, 56px);
    max-width: 16ch;
  }
  .problem-copy { margin-top: var(--space-3); }
  .problem-copy p + p { margin-top: var(--space-2); }
  @media (min-width: 860px) {
    .problem-statement {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(12, 1fr);
      column-gap: var(--space-4);
    }
    .problem-heading { grid-column: 1 / 8; }
    .problem-copy { grid-column: 9 / 13; margin-top: 0; }
  }

  .section-block { margin-top: var(--space-6); }
  .section-block h2 { margin-top: var(--space-2); }
  .section-block .prose { margin-top: var(--space-2); }
  .section-block .table-wrap { margin-top: var(--space-3); }
  .section-block ul.prose { padding-left: 1.2em; margin-top: var(--space-2); }
  .section-block ul.prose li { margin-top: 0.3em; }

  .product-grid {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .product-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  }

  .related ul { padding-left: 1.2em; margin-top: var(--space-1); }
  .related li { margin-top: 0.4em; }
</style>
